# Priority Hierarchy:
#   1. Google C++ Style Guide (google-*, misc-include-cleaner / IWYU)
#   2. Modern ISO C++23, ISO C23, and systems safety best practices
#
# Intentionally omitted checks:
#   - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters (noisy on symmetric DSA parameter pairs)
#   - bugprone-exception-escape (flags main() when ENABLE_EXCEPTIONS=ON)
#   - bugprone-random-generator-seed (tests intentionally use deterministic PRNG seeds)
#   - bugprone-signed-bitwise (uint8_t bit shifts promote to int under usual arithmetic conversions)
#   - cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory, cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-* (GSL banned; C23/systems pointer manipulation)
#   - cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-union-access (Crubit-generated Rust tagged enums expose C++ union members)
#   - misc-const-correctness (Google Style does not mandate const on every local value variable)
#   - misc-no-recursion (recursive LeetCode algorithms permitted; systems specs audit recursion explicitly)
#   - misc-use-anonymous-namespace (conflicts with C23 static internal linkage and misc-use-internal-linkage)
#   - modernize-use-integer-sign-comparison (signed/unsigned rule ignored per C++23 override)
#   - modernize-use-trailing-return-type (optional style preference)
#   - readability-function-cognitive-complexity (complex table/stress harnesses in tests and examples)
#   - readability-identifier-length (allows idiomatic math/loop indices)
#   - readability-identifier-naming (repo mixes CamelCase types with snake_case C++23/C23 library APIs)
#   - readability-magic-numbers (test fixtures and DSA constants)
#   - readability-trailing-comma (conflicts with Google clang-format)
#   - readability-uppercase-literal-suffix (C++23 0uz / 0z literals are lowercase per standard)
UseColor: true
WarningsAsErrors: "*"
# HeaderFilterRegex: '^(src)/.*'
Checks: "-*,
  abseil-cleanup-ctad,
  abseil-duration-addition,
  abseil-duration-comparison,
  abseil-duration-conversion-cast,
  abseil-duration-division,
  abseil-duration-factory-float,
  abseil-duration-factory-scale,
